@startuml
title R-ALLSTOP - Manual node-wide emergency stop (SH2+ target)
actor "Operator\nphone or terminal fallback" as Operator
participant "swarma-operator\noperator command; never harness account" as Control
participant "swarma-dispatcher" as Dispatcher
participant "swarma-user-manager" as Manager
participant "swarma-credential-broker" as Broker
participant "swarma-session-host" as Host
database "Host-private journal / fences" as State
participant "Bound boards (if any)" as Boards

Operator -> Control : one narrowing act; phone authentication + one confirmation, or password sudo fallback
note over Operator,Control
  R-OPERATOR: phone key never leaves hardware secure element; biometric presence.
  Exact act signed on phone; pinned key / canonical content verified; no signature reuse.
  Tailnet SSH into operator account; forced narrow operator command, no shell.
  Terminal: no NOPASSWD / cached ticket (timestamp_timeout=0).
  Refuse acts from agent sessions; observer account permits read-only status.
  Binary / wire / signature domain / canonical bytes unpublished (§7.16).
end note
Control -> Dispatcher : R-ALLSTOP operator act (format unpublished)
Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : journal hold; close admission
note over Dispatcher,Boards : Each service journals its own part; arrows do not publish a coordination wire or crash order.
Dispatcher -> Manager : deny-all agent / workplace UID range (R-RANGE-DENY)
Manager -> Manager : journal stop of every generation; account-wide scope / confirmed absence
Dispatcher -> Broker : freeze all leases and renewals
note over Broker : Tokens already delivered retain vendor lifetime.
Dispatcher -> Host : close delivery for every session
Host -> State : journal closed delivery fences; invalidate pending interactions
Host -> Boards : snapshot bound boards; no board required for goal-free session
alt Every required stop / snapshot / journal result known and absence confirmed
  Host -> State : record confirmed absence; keep stopped pending explicit recovery
else Partial / unknown result or absence unconfirmed
  Host -> State : retain fences and claims
  Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : keep admission closed
end
note over Dispatcher,Host
  Recovery is explicit, never automatic restart.
  R-LOCK: host holds state lock for local journal transitions only;
  board / dispatcher waits happen without the host state lock.
  R-WATCH never invokes this node-wide act automatically.
end note
legend bottom
  [[../spec/session-host.md#35-park-restart-emergency-stop-board-completion Spec §3.5: R-ALLSTOP / R-OPERATOR]]
  [[../spec/session-host.md#7-open-questions Spec §7.16: unpublished act and recovery]]
endlegend
@enduml
